WebAssembly Core Concepts
1. Module

Compiled WASM code.

calculator.wasm

Contains:

Functions
Memory
Tables
Globals
2. Instance

Running copy of a module.

const instance = result.instance;
3. Exports

Functions exposed to JavaScript.

Example:

int add(int a, int b);

JavaScript:

instance.exports.add()
4. Imports

JavaScript functions provided to WASM.

Example:

function log(x) {
   console.log(x);
}

WASM can call this.

5. Memory

Linear memory used by WASM.

new WebAssembly.Memory({
    initial: 1
});